rkusio/quarkus/issues/37662","id":1850581105,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCFbutM5uTaBx","user":{"login":"dmlloyd","id":124581,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNDU4MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124581?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd","html_url":"https://github.com/dmlloyd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-12-11T17:51:10Z","updated_at":"2023-12-11T17:51:10Z","body":"Rather than testing an exact time stamp string, the test checks that the date starts with `1970-`, presumably exactly because it expects an unknown time zone offset (however it wrongly assumes that the unknown time zone offset will always be positive, i.e. the test will not work in the Americas). I'm looking into what the actual cause for the difference between `Timestamp` and `Date` tests are (since the former passes and the latter does not).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/1850581105/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"dmlloyd","id":124581,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNDU4MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124581?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd","html_url":"https://github.com/dmlloyd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/1850623661","html_url":"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/37662#issuecomment-1850623661","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/37662","id":1850623661,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCFbutM5uTkat","user":{"login":"dmlloyd","id":124581,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNDU4MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124581?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd","html_url":"https://github.com/dmlloyd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-12-11T18:15:52Z","updated_at":"2023-12-11T18:17:28Z","body":"It looks like this problem is much worse than expected. Within Jackson we have this ominous note (see `com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.ser.std.SqlDateSerializer#serialize`):\r\n\r\n```java\r\n        // Alas, can't just call `_serializeAsString()`....\r\n        if (_customFormat == null) {\r\n            // 11-Oct-2016, tatu: For backwards-compatibility purposes, we shall just use\r\n            //    the awful standard JDK serialization via `sqlDate.toString()`... this\r\n            //    is problematic in multiple ways (including using arbitrary timezone...)\r\n            g.writeString(value.toString());\r\n            return;\r\n        }\r\n        _serializeAsString(value, g, provider);\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo, it is known that this result will reflect Jackson's basically incorrect behavior.\r\n\r\nThis gives us a few possible options:\r\n\r\nOption 1: Test the incorrect behavior to make sure it stays exactly as incorrect as it is now, but having the test pass in all time zones (i.e. \"fix the test\", and do regression testing only).\r\n\r\nOption 2: Drop the test, and say `java.sql.Date` is unsupported and must not be used.\r\n\r\nOption 2a: Just drop the test. Users are on their own.\r\n\r\nOption 3: Provide a \"correct\" serializer which converts the `java.sql.Date` into a local date by creating an `Instant` using the `getTime` epoch millis of the `Date`, and then gets the `LocalDate` of the `Instant` using the `UTC` time zone, serializing that value to string format. This will make the behavior \"correct\" (or as close to \"correct\" as can exist with `java.sql.Date`, which is a fundamentally broken type). It would require us to provide this custom conversion by default (I'm not sure how possible that is). \r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/1850623661/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket"